	(global_label "DAC_SYNC_N" (shape output) (at 55.88 88.9 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27))) (uuid "b9999999-9999-4999-8999-b99999999999"))
	(global_label "DAC_SDIN" (shape output) (at 60.96 88.9 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27))) (uuid "c1111111-1111-4111-8111-c11111111111"))
	(global_label "DAC_SDO" (shape input) (at 45.72 88.9 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27))) (uuid "c2222222-2222-4222-8222-c22222222222"))
	(global_label "DAC_LDAC_N" (shape input) (at 68.58 78.74 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27))) (uuid "c3333333-3333-4333-8333-c33333333333"))
	(global_label "DAC_CLR_N" (shape input) (at 68.58 53.34 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27))) (uuid "c4444444-4444-4334-8444-c44444444444"))
	(text "02_DAC_SOURCE_COMMAND rev0.2  AD5764ARUZ LQFP32 AVDD/AVSS= RAW +-12V_A (11.4V min) DVCC=+3V3  REFAB=REFCD=VREF_5V LTC6655-5.0\nDecoupling per DS: 100nF+10uF on AVDD/AVSS/DVCC within 2mm, REF 100nF+10uF. AGND/DGND star at plane. BIN=0 (offset binary). LDAC_N/CLR_N/RESET_N 10k PU to 3V3.\nSPI: SCLK/SYNC_N/SDIN/SDO to STM32G474 SPI2 (3.3V CMOS, 30MHz max). LDAC_N driven by MCU for synchronous update; CLR_N async zero. SDO readback provision.\nVOUTA..D +-10V span with REF 5V: Vout=4*VREF*(code/65536)-2*VREF => -10V(0x0000) 0V(0x8000) +10V(0xFFFF). For +-5V use half-codes 0x4000-0xC000 (305uV LSB).\nSlew RC: VOUTA -> R_SLEW 1k (DNP) + C_SLEW 1nF (DNP) -> VSET -> R_PD 100k to GND (safe 0V at POR). tau=1us (or 20us with 1k+10k trim). Mitigates R5.1 44% overshoot 0.1V step 10k/100p. Provision tune on prototype LDO?\nTP1 VREF_5V, TP2 DAC_VOUTA_raw, TP3 VSET_filtered, TP4 VCSRC, TP5 VCSNK, TP6/7/8 DAC VOUTB/C/D raw before conditioning.\nUnused channels: VOUTB/C/D have conditioning (B->VCSRC, C->VCSNK, D->spare/emergency thr) else NC with 10k to GND if DNP variant." (at 10 114.3 0) (effects (font (size 0.9 0.9))))
	(text "DAC Channel Allocation Table (AD5764 quad 16b)\nCh  Pin   Net DAC_xx_raw  Conditioned Net  Function                    Mapping/Notes\nA   10  VOUTA  DAC_VOUTA  -> VSET (via slew RC)  Primary voltage source VSET   -10..+10 -> -5..+5 limited half-codes; direct buffered to Kelvin servo +IN; 100k PD safe; RC DNP tune\nB   11  VOUTB  DAC_VOUTB  -> VCSRC (via 0.25x+2.5 clamp 0-5V)  Source current compliance Vc   DAC +-10 -> 0-5V clamp; 0V=0A min Icc safe; never negative; abs max 7V clamp BAT54S to +5V/GND; single-supply ADA4522 rail-limited\nC   12  VOUTC  DAC_VOUTC  -> VCSNK (via 0.25x+2.5 clamp 0-5V)  Sink current compliance Vc     same as B; independent source/sink per DEC-024\nD   13  VOUTD  DAC_VOUTD  -> Spare / TLV3501 emergency thr provision (or NC)  Emergency threshold 0-5V to comparator; default DNP threshold divider if not used\nNote: All channels share REFAB/REFCD=VREF_5V, REF_GND=AGND. BIN/2sC=0 offset binary matches FW half-code math. LDAC_N allows synchronous VSET+VCSx update. CLR_N pulses 0V." (at 10 127 0) (effects (font (size 0.9 0.9))))
	(text "VCSRC/VCSNK Conditioning Design (Level/Scale/Clamp 0-5V from +-10V DAC)\nTopology: DAC +-10V (20V span) -> precision divider+offset summing into ADA4522-1 non-inverting buffer (single +5V_A supply) -> 0-5V clamp to LT1970 Vc.\nTransfer: VCSRC = 0.25*VDAC + 2.5V  => -10V->0.0V, 0V->2.5V, +10V->5.0V. Implementation: VDAC through 30k (0.1% 25ppm) + VREF_5V through 30k + GND through 10k summing at +IN, feedback 20k sets gain 1.5x to hit 0.25 coeff.\nResistor spec: 0.1% 25ppm thin-film Susumu RG 0603, ratio matched to 0.02% effective (single batch). TC 25ppm*40C=0.1% worst; dominant error ~2.5mV at 5V (0.05%) trimmed by FW cal can be used together.\nClamp: BAT54S dual Schottky to +5V_A (anode at VCS, cathode to +5V) and to GND (cathode at VCS, anode to GND) + 100R series after opamp limits current; opamp single supply +5V_A cannot drive negative nor above +5V rail (headroom 100mV). Absolute max LT1970 Vc = 7V per 1970afc; clamp guarantees <5.3V.\nPower-up safe: DAC powers at code 0x0000 = -10V -> conditioning yields 0.0V (min compliance = min Icc); 100k PD on VSET and VCSx ensures 0V even if DAC high-Z; opamp pulldown via supply sequencing (POR 200ms). Never negative: diode to GND clamps at -0.3V.\nBW & noise: ADA4522 55nV/rtHz, RC at input 0.1uF? No extra cap; BW ~1MHz limited by feedback; filter cap DNP provision 100pF across Rf. Startup: VCSx tracks POR 200ms.\nCalibration: FW maps I_limit <-> VCS via per-range LUT using measured VREF_5V + DAC code; clamp voltage verified vs DMM at 0V/2.5V/5V." (at 10 142.24 0) (effects (font (size 0.85 0.85))))
)
